  "findings": [
    "v2 evaluates the statistics in float64 (`ResponseBatch` casts the float32 response matrix to float64; the case values are float32-representable, so both sides average the identical numbers) with one-hot design products instead of dictionary lookups. Only the summation order differs, so every step is exact (rtol 1e-12). Fallbacks agree on all test pairs: unseen sample, unseen tissue, unseen drug and unseen (drug, tissue) combination all predict the dataset mean plus the effects that are known (see `coverage` in the case metadata).",
    "1.6.1 falls back to `mean + cell line effect + drug effect` when the cell line features carry no tissue view. The v2 preset has `tissue: allow_missing`, which covers tissue annotations that are all missing (the `no_tissue` variant; same predictions), but a dataset whose `obs` lacks the `tissue` column entirely raises `KeyError: Sample column 'tissue' not found` in v2. Every shipped dataset has the column; recorded for completeness."
  ],
